# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Builder studio — local config (mode A, builder-studio.md §3.1).
#
#   cp apps/builder/.env.example apps/builder/.env
#   $EDITOR apps/builder/.env
#   pnpm builder dev --vertical demos/spike
#
# `.env` is gitignored by the recursive rule at .gitignore:25. Only this
# .example template is committed — same convention as secrets/*.env.example.
# Never commit a filled file.
#
# Two different kinds of thing live here, and it is worth keeping them straight:
#
#   CREDENTIALS are environment. Secret, per-machine, never committed. A real
#   shell variable always beats this file, so CI and one-off runs need no edits.
#
#   SETTINGS (which model, how deep a loop) are NOT secret. They are here only
#   as a convenience default for the terminal driver. Precedence is:
#       --model flag  →  SUBSTRAT_BUILDER_MODEL  →  the committed default
#   When the studio Worker and chat pane land, model choice becomes a per-session
#   UI setting stored with the session, not an env var — two builders will want
#   different models, and switching mid-session is legitimate.
#
# These apply to the LOCAL Node driver only. The studio Worker's credentials will
# be real worker secrets via scripts/secrets.mjs, not this file.
#
# The key is never forwarded into the workspace: LocalWorkspace builds a minimal
# env for `exec`, so the agent's shell cannot read it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═══ CREDENTIALS — set the one for the provider you intend to use ════════════

# ── Claude (default provider) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   pnpm builder dev --model anthropic:claude-opus-5
# Create a key at https://platform.claude.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Qwen, via Alibaba Model Studio (DashScope), OpenAI-compatible mode ───────
#   pnpm builder dev --model qwen:qwen3-coder-plus
#
# Use the OpenAI-compatible URL (…/compatible-mode/v1) — that is the dialect this
# provider speaks. An Anthropic-compatible endpoint is NOT needed.
#
# Keys are region- AND workspace-scoped: a key minted in one console returns a
# plain 401 against another region's endpoint, so match these two to each other.
#   international (default) https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
#   China mainland          https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
#   US                      https://dashscope-us.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
#   workspace plan          https://<workspace>.<region>.maas.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
# DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=
# DASHSCOPE_BASE_URL=https://token-plan.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1

# ── Cloudflare Workers AI, OpenAI-compatible mode ────────────────────────────
#   pnpm builder dev --model cloudflare:@cf/zai-org/glm-5.2
#
# The endpoint is account-scoped — fill in your account id:
#   https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/<account-id>/ai/v1
# The token needs the Workers AI permission. Deliberately NOT wrangler's
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, so an ambient deploy token is never silently used.
#
# Model ids keep their full catalog prefix. Coding models:
#   @cf/zai-org/glm-5.2 · @cf/zai-org/glm-4.7-flash ·
#   @cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code ·
#   deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro (partner-served, unified billing)
# CLOUDFLARE_AI_BASE_URL=
# CLOUDFLARE_AI_API_TOKEN=

# ── Local models via Ollama — no credential needed ───────────────────────────
#   ollama serve && ollama pull qwen3-coder
#   pnpm builder dev --model ollama:qwen3-coder
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# ── Any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint (vLLM, LM Studio, OpenRouter…) ──────
#   pnpm builder dev --model compat:<model-id>
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URL=
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_API_KEY=

# ── Direct providers — each needs its package installed first ────────────────
#   pnpm add --filter @substrat-run/builder @ai-sdk/openai
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=

# Optional endpoint overrides for the two direct providers that support one —
# only for a proxy or gateway. Leave unset to use the vendor's own endpoint.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=


# ═══ SETTINGS — not secret; override per run with a flag ═════════════════════

# Default model for `pnpm builder dev` on this machine. Form: provider:model.
# Overridden by --model. Omit to use the committed default (anthropic:claude-opus-5).
# SUBSTRAT_BUILDER_MODEL=qwen:qwen3-coder-plus
